  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Note: </strong>Aldosterone levels are affected by recent sodium intake and posture. This reference range pertains to normal salt&nbsp;intake.</p>\n<p><br><strong>Clinical Use</strong><br>&bull;Assess Adrenal Aldosterone production<br>&bull;Diagnose Primary Hyperaldosteronism due to Adrenal adenoma or bilateral Adrenal Hyperplasia</p>\n<p><br><strong>Increased Levels</strong><br>Primary Hyperaldosteronism, Secondary hyperaldosteronism, Very Low Sodium diet, Pregnancy, Bartter Syndrome</p>\n<p><br><strong>Decreased Levels</strong><br>Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia, Aldosterone synthetase deficiency, Very high sodium diet, Addison&rsquo;s disease, Hyporeninemic&nbsp;hypoaldosteronism, Adrenal hypoplasia</p>",
